.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_HEADER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_header \- look up a request header
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

const char *chttpsvr_req_header(const chttpsvr_req *req,
                                 const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the value of the request header called name, or NULL when that
header is absent.  The lookup is case-insensitive, and when a header
appears more than once the last value is returned.

The pointer stays valid for the duration of the handler call.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The trailer fields of a chunked request body (RFC 7230 4.1.2) are not
request headers, and this function never returns one: it answers only
from the header block of the request, so a trailer field of any name
reads as absent, on buffered and streaming routes alike.

Trailer fields arrive after the server has routed the request and
after the middleware has run, and on a buffered route also after the
server has read the header block.  Indexing trailers alongside headers
would therefore let a client add a trailer that displaces a header set
by an upstream proxy (such as X-Forwarded-For, or the identity header
of an authentication gateway) on a request the server has already
committed to.  This server has no trailer accessor at all; a
deployment that needs trailer semantics should terminate the trailers
in front of this server.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_method (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_path (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_read (3)
